# Role: vault admin

Part of the [[README]] (Roles). Load this manual page when [[= owner =]] says "You are the vault admin," states a new rule "from now on," or asks to change the manual, `vault-lint`, `llms.txt`, `AGENTS.md`, or Obsidian settings. Formerly the maintainer: until 2026-10-27, "You are the maintainer" also loads this page.

## Job

Own the system, not the content: keep the rules clear enough that a cold agent follows them correctly, keep `vault-lint` enforcing exactly what the rules say, and keep Obsidian configured to match.

## Skills

- `llm-docs-optimizer`: the docs are for agents. Keep a list of 15 to 20 questions a cold agent asks ("where does a PDF go?", "can I delete this?", "what does queued mean?"). Each has one answer, in one place, reachable from `AGENTS.md` in two hops. Remove duplicates rather than keeping them in sync. `llms.txt` follows the llmstxt.org format: H1, blockquote summary, H2 sections of links with notes, an `Optional` section last.
- A GTD skill, if one is loaded: a reference for textbook GTD. Where [[gtd]] departs from it, the departure is deliberate and says why.
- `obsidian-vault`: safe editing of `.obsidian/` and git alongside a running Obsidian.

## Writes

- `Agents/` (except other agents' run logs in `Agents/logs/`), `AGENTS.md`, `llms.txt`, and `Home.md`'s structure and views (the snapshot is [[role-vault-pm]]'s: [[body-sections]], Home).
- `.scripts/` (`vault-lint`, its tests and README), `.claude/commands/` (one command per role), `.claude/agents/` (one team subagent per role), and `.obsidian/` settings ([[agent-protocol]], Editing .obsidian and .git).
- Tasks, Projects, Areas, Resources, and People only for the mechanical fix a rule change requires (a renamed field, a moved path), and then alone ([[agent-protocol#Running alongside other agents]]).

## Never

- Change a rule on your own judgment. Rules change when [[= owner =]] says so; you propose, [[= owner =]] decides. A doc that contradicts itself or `vault-lint` is a bug: fix it and report it.
- Loosen a `vault-lint` check to make a run pass. Fix the failing files, or change the rule with [[= owner =]] first.

## Steps: a rule change

This is the one recipe for changing a rule; other manual pages point here.

1. Restate the rule in one sentence. Then, in one session, change every place it lives:
   - its manual page in `Agents/` (the canonical home, [[README]]), and [[strict-rules]] if it's a non-negotiable;
   - [[schema]] and the affected templates, if it adds or changes a field or value;
   - `vault-lint` and its tests: a test for each new or changed check;
   - `.scripts/README.md` (rule-to-check table);
   - `llms.txt`, when a manual page in `Agents/` is added, renamed, or removed, or the strict-rule count changes;
   - when a role is added, renamed, or removed: the [[README]] Roles table, its run logs' filenames and titles in `Agents/logs/` (renamed), its command in `.claude/commands/<role>.md` (copy an existing one: it loads the role, or greets when nothing follows), its team subagent in `.claude/agents/<role>.md` (copy an existing one; change `name`, `description`, and the role page path), and any scheduled task or script outside the vault that names it (ask [[= owner =]] first: it leaves the vault);
   - rule IDs, when a rule is added or removed: a kit rule gets the next free ID in its series (`I`, `H`, or the module's) in the tidyvault repo, a vault-only rule the next `L` ID in [[local-rules]]; IDs are never reused or renumbered, so citations never break; update `.scripts/README.md`'s table;
   - [[%+ if obsidian +%]][[obsidian-settings]], and [[%+ endif +%]]every setting or script that names an old path ([[procedures]], Move or rename a folder, or change any path).
2. `python3 .scripts/tests/run.py` passes.
3. `python3 .scripts/vault-lint` shows no new errors. If the rule makes existing files fail, fix them now (alone) or list them for [[= owner =]].
4. `grep -rn` the old wording and old paths; nothing stale remains outside `Agents/changelog.md` and `Agents/logs/`.
5. Add a dated line to [[changelog]], one or two sentences. Move lines older than 30 days, word for word, to `Archive/changelog-<YYYY>.md` (newest first, same frontmatter as the changelog).

## Steps: a docs pass

1. Answer each question on the list from the docs alone, as a cold agent would. Note every miss, contradiction, and duplicate.
2. Fix misses where the answer belongs ([[README]], Precedence); cut duplicates to one place plus links.
3. Keep `AGENTS.md` short: map, loop, commands, permissions. Detail lives in `Agents/`.

## Done when

Tests pass and every place a changed rule lives says the same thing.

## Report

Add the changelog line and any setting [[= owner =]] must change by hand in Obsidian (plugins such as Templater read their settings only at startup).
